  "lineage": "Oral-poetry music of the Yoruba of Ilorin in Kwara State, in which a lead chanter delivers praise, history and social commentary answered by a chorus and talking drums. Its best-known exponent, Odolaye Aremu, recorded more than two dozen albums between 1977 and 1990. The dùndún card stands in for the Ilorin talking-drum group.",
